            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Top-freezer refrigerators are generally the most reliable because they have the fewest parts: two doors, one compressor and usually no dispenser. Bottom-freezers come next. Side-by-side and French door models usually add through-the-door ice and water dispensers and extra doors, which owners and repair technicians commonly link to more service calls."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are ice makers really that unreliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Ice makers are among the most common reasons a refrigerator needs service, because they rely on a water valve, fill tube, motor, heater and sensor. Hard water and low water pressure make problems more likely. If reliability matters most, buy a model without one or an ice maker ready model and add a kit only if you need it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is LG or Samsung more reliable for refrigerators?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both brands sell many complex French door and four-door models with dispensers, and both have faced owner complaints about ice makers on some models. If you buy either brand for reliability, choose a simpler layout such as a top-freezer or bottom-freezer, compare compressor warranty terms and check whether an authorized technician is available near you."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long should a refrigerator last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Many basic refrigerators run well past a decade with routine care such as cleaning the condenser coils and keeping door gaskets in good shape. Simpler layouts tend to last longer than feature-heavy ones. Repair costs, energy use and the age of the unit decide whether fixing an older refrigerator makes more sense than replacing it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does a longer compressor warranty mean a more reliable refrigerator?",
