            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not necessarily, but it shows the maker's confidence and reduces your risk on the costliest part. Read the terms closely. Many long compressor warranties cover parts only, so you still pay the technician to open and recharge the sealed system. Compare parts and labor coverage separately for each model you are considering."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I buy an extended warranty on a refrigerator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on complexity. On a simple top-freezer with few parts, an extended plan rarely pays off. On a French door or side-by-side with a dispenser and ice maker, it can make more sense. Before buying, check who performs repairs, the deductible, and whether the plan replaces the unit after repeated failures."
          }
